{"id":"word:hebrew:H5553","type":"word","title":"סֶלַע","subtitle":"H5553 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a craggy rock , literally or figuratively (a fortress )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to סֶלַע (H5553) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 59 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"סֶלַע (çelaʻ) means a craggy rock , literally or figuratively (a fortress ) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 19 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"סֶלַע","transliteration":"çelaʻ","pronunciation":"seh'-lah","strong":"H5553","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5553","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["סֶ֣לַע","הַ/סֶּ֔לַע","הַ/סָּֽלַע","הַ/סָּ֑לַע","סַֽלְעִ֥/י"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",16],["HNcmsa",12],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",5],["HRd/Ncmsa",5],["HTd/Ncmpa",5],["HR/Ncmsa",4],["HNcmsc",4],["HNcmpa",3],["HR/Ncmsc",2],["HC/Rd/Ncmpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a craggy rock , literally or figuratively (a fortress )","usage":"(ragged) rock, stone(-ny), strong hold.","full":"H5553. sela I. סֶ֫לַע 61 noun masculine Judg 6:20 crag, cliff , synonym צוּר ; — absolute ׳ס 6:20 +, סָ֑לַע Num 20:10 +; construct סֶ֫לַע 1Sam 23:28 ; suffix סַלְעִי 2Sam 22:2 +, סַלְעוֺ Isa 31:9 ; plural סְלָעִים 2:21 +; — 1 literally cliff, crag Judg 6:20 ; Isa 2:21 ; 7:19 ; Amos 6:12 ; Num 20:8 (twice in verse); 20:10 (twice in verse); 20:11 (compare Neh 9:15 ; Psa 78:16 , and contrast the צוּר of Exod 17:6 ), Num 24:21 ; Deut 32:13 (not elsewhere Hexateuch), + 10 t.; הַסּ ׳שֵׁן 1Sam 14:4 (twice in verse) tooth of the crag , i.e. sharp crag, so Job 39:28 ; excavated in cliff as place of burial Isa 22:16 ; abode of wild animals, ׳יַעֲלֵיסֿ 22:1 , compare Psa 104:18 ; Prov 30:26 , of birds Job 39:28 ; Song 2:14 (in figurative), compare Jer 48:28 , so of Edom Obadiah 3 = 49:16 ; compare ( Num 24:21 above and) Isa 42:11 ; particular cliffs are: ׳ס עֵיטָם Judg 15:8 , 11 compare 15:13 , ׳ס (הָ)רִמּוֺן 20:45 , 47 (twice in verse); 21:13 ׳ס הַמַּחְלְקוֺת 1Sam 23:28 compare 23:25 ; see also II. סֶלַע . 2 figurative, especially סַלְעִי of ׳י (only Psalms), Psa 18:3 = 2Sam 22:2 ; Psa 31:4 ; 42:10 ; 71:3 ; of Assyrian god Isa 31:9 (probably; compare צוּר Deut 32:31 , 37 ); ס ׳צֵל כָּבֵד Isa 32:2 (simile of protecting care); figurative of security Psa 40:3 (feet on cliff), מִשְׂגַּבּוֺ סְלָעִים מְצָדוֺת Isa 33:16 ; symbol of obstinacy מִסּ פְנֵיהֶם ׳חִזְּקוּ Jer 5:3 ; ס ׳צְחִיחַ ( bare cliff , literally glare of [ the ] cliff ), in figure of openness, flagrancy Ezek 24:7-8 , of razed city 26:4 , 14 (only here Ezekiel); in figure of fall of Babylonian Jer 51:25 .","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to be lofty ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 19 11","keyReferences":["1Kgs 19 11","1Sam 13 6","1Sam 14 4","1Sam 14 4","1Sam 23 25","2Chr 25 12","2Chr 25 12","2Sam 22 2"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":59,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 19 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":19,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"סְלָעִים֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"1Sam 13 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":13,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בַ/סְּלָעִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Rd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/סֶּ֤לַע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/סֶּ֥לַע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 23 25","book":"1Sam","chapter":23,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/סֶּ֔לַע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 25 12","book":"2Chr","chapter":25,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/סָּ֑לַע","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 25 12","book":"2Chr","chapter":25,"verse":12,"engli